 proximity of these stores to Lincoln Park in Chicago.\\n\\n```python\\nimport geopy.distance\\n\\ndef verify_geographic_proximity(store_address, reference_address=\"Lincoln Park, Chicago, IL\"):\\n    from geopy.geocoders import Nominatim\\n    geolocator = Nominatim(user_agent=\"geo_verification\")\\n    \\n    location_reference = geolocator.geocode(reference_address)\\n    location_store = geolocator.geocode(store_address)\\n    \\n    coords_reference = (location_reference.latitude, location_reference.longitude)\\n    coords_store = (location_store.latitude, location_store.longitude)\\n    \\n    distance = geopy.distance.distance(coords_reference, coords_store).miles\\n    \\n    # Convert miles to blocks (assuming 20 blocks per mile)\\n    distance_in_blocks = distance * 20\\n    return distance_in_blocks\\n\\n# Addresses of the supermarkets\\naddresses = {\\n    \"Whole Foods Market\": \"1550 N Kingsbury St, Chicago, IL 60642\",\\n    \"Costco\": \"2746 N Clybourn Ave, Chicago, IL 60614\",\\n    \"Menards\": \"2601 N Clybourn Ave, Chicago, IL 60614\"\\n}\\n\\nproximities = {store: verify_geographic_proximity(address) for store, address in addresses.items()}\\n\\nfor store, blocks in proximities.items():\\n    print(f\"{store} is approximately {blocks:.2f} blocks from Lincoln Park, Chicago, IL.\")\\n```\\n\\nLet\\'s run the verification code and interpret the results to confirm the proximity of these supermarkets to Lincoln Park.\\n\\nIf the proximities are confirmed to be within 2 blocks and the prices are accurately listed under $15, we can conclude that the information is accurate. If there are discrepancies, we will correct the information accordingly.', 'name': 'Verification_Expert', 'role': 'user'}}, {'step': 3, 'agent': 'Computer_terminal', 'message': {'content': 'exitcode: 0 (execution succeeded)\\nCode output: Whole Foods Market is approximately 46.79 blocks from Lincoln Park, Chicago, IL.\\nCostco is approximately 45.31 blocks from Lincoln Park, Chi